This is the top portion of a screenshot of a web page that was just captured. Classify the LOADING STATE:
- 'ok': page loaded, shows real content (text, images, readable layout);
- 'black': mostly black/dark with no content;
- 'blank': mostly empty/white with no content;
- 'loading': shows a spinner, skeleton, a counter/percentage or a loading screen;
- 'partial': only partially loaded (large empty areas, missing images/sections).
Provide a status and a very short reason.

